<title>USA: Chevron shutting refinery due to hurricane.</title>
<headline>Chevron shutting refinery due to hurricane.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chevron Corp said it is in the process of shutting its 295,000 barrel per day refinery in Pascagoula, Mississippi as a precautionary measure to Hurricane Danny.</p>
<p>&quot;We expect the refinery to be secured by 6 pm tonight,&quot; said Steve Renfroe, Chevron spokesman.  </p>
<p>Renfroe said Chevron did not know when the refinery would come back up as it depended on the path of the Hurricane.</p>
<p>The hurricane was moving northeast across the tip of Louisiana early Friday at five miles per hour with maximum sustained with winds of 75 miles per hour.</p>
<p>-- New York Energy Desk, 212-859-1620</p>
</text>
